meta {
  name: Search Policies
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/policies/search?q=&limit=20
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

params:query {
  ~q:
  limit: 20
  ~householdId: {{householdId}}
}

headers {
  ~X-Branch-Id: {{branchId}}
}

tests {
  test("returns 200 OK", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(200);
  });

  test("returns a list of PolicySearchResult", function () {
    const body = res.getBody();
    expect(body).to.be.an("array");
    if (body.length) {
      expect(body[0]).to.have.property("id");
      expect(body[0]).to.have.property("policyNumber");
      expect(body[0]).to.have.property("householdId");
      expect(body[0]).to.have.property("householdName");
    }
  });

  test("householdId, when sent, returns only that household's policies", function () {
    const householdId = bru.getVar("householdId") || bru.getEnvVar("householdId");
    if (!householdId || !req.getUrl().includes("householdId")) return;
    res.getBody().forEach(function (policy) {
      expect(policy.householdId).to.equal(householdId);
    });
  });
}

docs {
  # GET /policies/search

  Typeahead behind the **Policy** picker in the *New Service Ticket* dialog.

  - **Module:** `clients` **OR** `crm_service` (class-level `@RequireAnyModule`).
  - **Permission:** `clients:read` **OR** `crm_service:read` — policies render
    both on the Clients pages and inside the CRM ticket detail.
  - **Data scope:** `agency` sees the agency; `branch` **and `own`** both
    collapse to the caller's branch, because client records are shared and carry
    no per-user owner.

  ## Query params
  | Param | Required | Notes |
  |---|---|---|
  | `q` | no | Case-insensitive match on `policyNumber`, `policyType`, or `carrier`. Blank/omitted returns the first page unfiltered, so the picker has rows before the user types. Regex-escaped — a term is never compiled as a pattern |
  | `limit` | no | 1–50, default 20 |
  | `householdId` | no | Mongo id. Restricts results to that household's policies |

  ### `householdId` — who sends it, and why
  The New Ticket dialog opened from a **household page** (`/clients/:id`) sends
  it; opened from the Service Dashboard it does not. On a client's own page the
  ticket is being filed *for that client*, so offering the whole agency's book
  is both noise and a chance to link someone else's policy to the ticket.

  A well-formed id that is out of the caller's scope (another agency or branch)
  returns `[]` — **never** the unfiltered list. Silently widening on an id the
  caller cannot see would defeat the filter exactly when it matters.

  ## Response
  `PolicySearchResult[]` — `PolicySummary` plus `householdId` / `householdName`,
  resolved in one extra round-trip so the picker can show the owning client as a
  row hint. Sorted `active` first, then by policy number.

  ## Errors
  | Status | When |
  |---|---|
  | 400 | `limit` outside 1–50, `q` over 120 chars, or a malformed `householdId` |
  | 401 | Missing/expired bearer token |
  | 403 | Both `clients` and `crm_service` disabled, or the caller holds neither read permission |
}
